From: LinuxCNC AI Curriculum source-review draft (NOT upstream submitted)
Subject: [PATCH DRAFT] xhc-whb04b-6: distinguish ordinary RESET/STOP and USB connection from protective safety
Base: LinuxCNC/linuxcnc v2.9.10 (source-only, not runtime tested)
---
diff --git a/docs/src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc b/docs/src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc
--- a/docs/src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc
+++ b/docs/src/man/man1/xhc-whb04b-6.1.adoc
@@ -304,8 +304,9 @@
 `whb.button.reset` (bit,out)::
- see `whb.halui.estop.`{`activate`, `reset`}
- True one Reset button down, false otherwise.
- For toggling E-stop use whb.halui.estop .active and .reset.
+ True while the RESET button is held, false otherwise.
+ The built-in handler requests ordinary machine ON/OFF through `whb.halui.machine.on/off`.
+ This is not an independent personnel-protective E-stop or safety reset.
 `whb.button.stop` (bit,out)::
  see `whb.halui.program.stop`. True on Stop button down, false otherwise.
- For stopping a program use `whb.halui.program.stop`.
+ The built-in handler requests ordinary Task abort through `whb.halui.program.stop`.
+ This does not establish a personnel-protective stop or physical standstill.
 `whb.button.start-pause` (bit,out)::
@@ -396,5 +397,5 @@
 `whb.pendant.is-sleeping` (bit,out)::
- True as long pendant is in sleep mode (usually a few seconds after turned off), false otherwise.
+ Reports sleep state inferred from received pendant packets; not a safety-rated link monitor.
 `whb.pendant.is-connected` (bit,out)::
- True as long pendant is not in sleep mode (turned on), false otherwise.
+ Set after USB receiver initialization succeeds; not proof of a live wireless link or safe machine state.
 
diff --git a/src/hal/user_comps/xhc-whb04b-6/hal.h b/src/hal/user_comps/xhc-whb04b-6/hal.h
--- a/src/hal/user_comps/xhc-whb04b-6/hal.h
+++ b/src/hal/user_comps/xhc-whb04b-6/hal.h
@@ -386,5 +386,5 @@
-    //! Sets the hal state of the respective pin (reset). Usually called in case the reset
-    //! button is pressed or released. The pin should be connected to \ref halui.estop.activate.
+    //! Sets the raw RESET button pin and requests ordinary machine ON/OFF through
+    //! the component's built-in handler. This is not a personnel-safety E-stop.
     //! \param enabled the new pin value, (true if the button was pressed, false otherwise)
     //! \ref Hal::halInit(const WhbSoftwareButton* , size_t , const WhbKeyCodes&)
     //! \sa setReset(bool)
